arf","Space"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-10T19:36:22Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-mit-star-brown-dwarf-0-af41de5d-9a4a-4a55-a0dc-a4eeb1963a6c.webp","alt":"Illustration of mass transfer in a binary system: a brown dwarf feeding a red dwarf star","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"MIT Kavli Institute press release — astronomers catch a star slowly snacking on a brown dwarf 300 light-years away","url":"https://www.space.mit.edu/news/astronomers-catch-a-star-slowly-snacking-on-a-brown-dwarf-300-light-years-away/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Phys.org — astronomers catch a star slowly snacking on a brown dwarf","url":"https://phys.org/news/2026-10-astronomers-star-slowly-snacking-brown.html","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"MIT Kavli Institute press release opened and read: announced October 5, 2026; led by Kevin Burdge and Aaron Householder; system ZTF J0440+2325 ~300 light-years away, found via Zwicky Transient Facility at Palomar; star ~85 Jupiter masses, brown dwarf ~25; 86.65-minute orbit; accretion ~1/100,000 Earth mass per year; could continue hundreds of thousands to billions of years; Nature Astronomy paper 'Stable mass transfer from a substellar object onto an M dwarf' (DOI 10.1038/s41550-026-02992-6). Phys.org version corroborates. No superseding development at check time.","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T19:36:22Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":true,"pinUrl":"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1125618500654698417/"},{"id":"art-0018-hurricane-isaias-florida-2026","slug":"hurricane-isaias-florida-landfall-2026","headline":"Hurricane Isaias Kills at Least 4 and Leaves Hundreds of Thousands Without Power After Florida Landfall","socialHeadline":"Category 2 Hurricane Isaias slammed into the Florida panhandle near Destin — at least 4 dead and 400,000+ without power as the storm moved inland","summary":"Hurricane Isaias made landfall near Destin, Florida, as a Category 2 storm on October 9, killing at least four people and knocking out power to hundreds of thousands across the Florida panhandle, Alabama and western Georgia before weakening to a post-tropical cyclone.","body":["Hurricane Isaias came ashore near Destin, Florida, on the evening of October 9 as a Category 2 hurricane with sustained winds of 105 miles per hour, tearing across the Florida panhandle and into Alabama and Georgia before the National Hurricane Center downgraded it to a post-tropical cyclone and issued its final advisory.","At least four people were killed — two in Alabama, confirmed by Governor Kay Ivey, and two in Florida, confirmed by the Escambia County sheriff. Between 400,000 and more than 560,000 homes and businesses lost power across the Florida panhandle, Alabama and western Georgia, according to utility reports cited in live storm coverage.","Florida Governor Ron DeSantis and state emergency officials coordinated the response as Florida Power & Light and other utilities began damage assessments and restoration work. The storm's heaviest impacts were felt around the landfall zone near Destin, where high winds downed trees and power lines.","## Why it matters","Isaias is the most destructive Gulf hurricane of the 2026 season so far, and recovery in the panhandle will take days as crews work through widespread outages."],"category":"World","tags":["Hurricane Isaias","Florida","Weather","US"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T02:02:17.739Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-isaias-landfall-v2-0-2bf18423-4bbc-4395-9b9d-82eccf25fe73.webp","alt":"Illustration of a hurricane symbol over a simplified Florida panhandle coastline map","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"USA Today — Hurricane Isaias live updates (citing NHC/NWS data, Gov. Ron DeSantis, Florida Power & Light, Alabama Gov. Kay Ivey)","url":"https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/weather/2026/10/10/hurricane-isaias-live-updates-forecast--live/92172297007/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Pensacola News Journal — Hurricane Isaias live updates (citing National Hurricane Center)","url":"https://www.pnj.com/story/weather/hurricanes/2026/10/10/updates-hurricane-isaias-florida-pensacola-damage-today--live/92188656007/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"USA Today live-updates page opened and read: landfall near Destin FL ~8:30pm CT Oct 9 as Cat 2 (105 mph); downgraded to post-tropical with NHC final advisory; 4 dead (2 Alabama per Gov. Kay Ivey, 2 Florida per Escambia County sheriff); 400,000-560,000+ without power across FL panhandle, Alabama, western Georgia. Pensacola News Journal corroborates landfall details and NHC data. No superseding development at check time.","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T02:02:17.739Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":true,"pinUrl":"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1125618500654698444/"},{"id":"art-0019-oklahoma-texas-red-river-2026","slug":"oklahoma-stuns-no1-texas-red-river-2026","headline":"Oklahoma Stuns No. 1 Texas 27-24 on Sandell's Last-Second Field Goal in Red River Rivalry","socialHeadline":"Tate Sandell's 47-yard field goal on the final play sealed Oklahoma's 27-24 upset of No. 1 Texas — the Sooners' first win over a top-ranked team since 2007","summary":"Oklahoma upset No. 1 Texas 27-24 in the Red River Rivalry at the Cotton Bowl on October 10, winning on Tate Sandell's 47-yard field goal on the final play of the game.","body":["Oklahoma stunned No. 1 Texas 27-24 in the Red River Rivalry at the Cotton Bowl in Dallas on Saturday, October 10, as kicker Tate Sandell drilled a 47-yard field goal on the final play to hand the Longhorns their first loss of the season.","Quarterback John Mateer engineered the winning drive, completing 13- and 20-yard passes to Isaiah Sategna to move the Sooners into field-goal range in the closing seconds. It was Oklahoma's first victory over a No. 1-ranked team since 2007.","Texas quarterback Arch Manning threw three touchdowns but was intercepted twice at decisive moments — Peyton Bowen returned one 42 yards for a pick-six, and Omarion Robinson intercepted Manning with 19 seconds left to set up the final drive. Texas (4-1) had entered the game unbeaten; Oklahoma improved to 3-2.","## Why it matters","The upset scrambles the College Football Playoff picture and gives Oklahoma a signature win in a rivalry that rarely disappoints."],"category":"Sports","tags":["College Football","Oklahoma","Texas","Red River Rivalry"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T02:02:17.739Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-oklahoma-texas-v2-0-27824912-f5f0-4a8b-95d3-be66c248d81f.webp","alt":"Illustration of an American football arcing toward goalposts under stadium lights","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"ESPN College Football — Oklahoma stuns No. 1 Texas on last-second FG (Red River)","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50151802/oklahoma-stuns-no-1-texas-last-second-fg-red-river","role":"primary"},{"name":"NBC Sports — Oklahoma upsets No. 1 Texas on Tate Sandell's game-ending 47-yard field goal","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/college-football/news/oklahoma-upsets-no-1-texas-on-tate-sandells-game-ending-47-yard-field-goal","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"ESPN discovery feed item matched the confirmed event (story slug itself describes the outcome); ESPN pages were not directly fetchable by the verification tool (domain blocked), so all decisive facts were confirmed via the NBC Sports game report opened and read: 27-24 final, Cotton Bowl Dallas Oct 10, Sandell 47-yard FG on final play, Mateer 13- and 20-yard passes to Sategna, Manning 3 TDs/2 INTs (Bowen 42-yard pick-six, Robinson INT with 0:19 left), Oklahoma 3-2 first win over No. 1 since 2007, Texas 4-1 first loss. No superseding development at check time.","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T02:02:17.739Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":true,"pinUrl":"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1125618500654698465/"},{"id":"art-0020-vinicius-red-card-villarreal-2026","slug":"vinicius-red-card-hair-pull-villarreal-2026","headline":"Vinicius Apologises After Red Card for Hair Pull in Real Madrid's Win Over Villarreal","socialHeadline":"Sent off for pulling Nathan Saliba's hair, Vinicius Jr faces a ban that could rule him out of El Clasico — and he has apologised to the team and fans","summary":"Real Madrid forward Vinicius Jr was sent off for pulling Villarreal defender Nathan Saliba's hair during Madrid's 1-0 LaLiga win on October 10, and faces a suspension that could rule him out of the El Clasico against Barcelona.","body":["Real Madrid's Vinicius Jr was shown a straight red card during Saturday's 1-0 LaLiga win over Villarreal at the Santiago Bernabeu after pulling the hair of Villarreal defender Nathan Saliba. The Brazilian, who had come on as a 52nd-minute substitute, was dismissed about 20 minutes later.","The incident overshadowed the match: a Real Madrid goal that would have made it 2-0 was disallowed after a VAR review in the same passage of play. Vinicius later apologised on social media, saying sorry to the team and the fans.","Under Spanish football federation rules on violent conduct (Article 130), the forward faces a suspension of one to three matches — a ban that could rule him out of the El Clasico against Barcelona at Camp Nou on October 25. Madrid's upcoming fixtures also include Sevilla and Racing Santander.","## Why it matters","Losing Vinicius for the season's first Clasico would be a major blow to Real Madrid's title ambitions."],"category":"Sports","tags":["LaLiga","Real Madrid","Vinicius Jr","Football"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T02:02:17.739Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-vinicius-redcard-0-941f7f01-6ae4-42c3-8f69-16a44d685727.webp","alt":"Illustration of a referee's red card over abstract football pitch markings","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"CNA Sport — Real's Vinicius apologises after red card for hair pull against Villarreal","url":"https://www.channelnewsasia.com/sport/reals-vinicius-apologises-after-red-card-hair-pull-against-villarreal-6449791","role":"primary"},{"name":"Reuters — Real's Vinicius apologises after red card for hair pull against Villarreal","url":"https://www.reuters.com/sports/soccer/reals-vinicius-apologises-after-red-card-hair-pull-against-villarreal-2026-10-10/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"CNA page opened and read: red card for hair pull on Nathan Saliba, came on 52nd min, sent off ~20 min later, Bernabeu 1-0 win Oct 10, apology ('sorry to the team and the fans'), possible El Clasico absence. Reuters corroborates: VAR-disallowed goal in the same passage, 1-3 match ban under RFEF Art. 130 violent conduct, El Clasico Oct 25 at Camp Nou, next fixtures Sevilla/Barca/Racing Santander. No superseding development at check time.","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T02:02:17.739Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":true,"pinUrl":"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1125618500654698487/"},{"id":"art-0021-gaza-ceasefire-protests-2026","slug":"global-protests-mark-gaza-ceasefire-anniversary-2026","headline":"Thousands March Worldwide Marking One Year Since Gaza Ceasefire","socialHeadline":"From London to Berlin to New York, thousands joined pro-Palestinian marches one year after the Gaza ceasefire took effect","summary":"Thousands of pro-Palestinian demonstrators marched in cities including London, Berlin, New York, Athens and Dublin on October 10, marking one year since the Gaza ceasefire took effect.","body":["Thousands of pro-Palestinian demonstrators took to the streets in cities across Europe and the United States on Saturday, October 10, to mark one year since the Gaza ceasefire took effect.","In London, thousands marched on a route near parliament in a demonstration organised by the Palestine Coalition; police said 20 people were arrested, and a small pro-Israel counter-demonstration also took place. In Berlin, police estimated around 3,500 participants in a march organised by United for Palestine. Demonstrations were also reported in New York, Athens and Dublin, where the Irish Palestine Solidarity Campaign organised a rally.","Organisers said the marches were intended to press for a lasting peace. The Gaza health ministry says around 1,450 Palestinians have been killed by Israeli strikes since the ceasefire began.","## Why it matters","The anniversary marches show the Gaza conflict remains a potent force in street politics a year after the ceasefire, with organisers vowing to keep pressure on governments."],"category":"World","tags":["Gaza","Protests","Ceasefire","Middle East"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T02:02:17.739Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-gaza-ceasefire-protests-0-a92847ff-bfd8-435a-a373-4b55c6c74222.webp","alt":"Illustration of abstract demonstrators holding blank placards beneath an olive branch","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Al Jazeera — Global protests for Gaza solidarity (newsfeed)","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/10/11/11-10-sv-global-protests-for-gaza-solidarity-uk?traffic_source=rss","role":"primary"},{"name":"AFP wire (republished) — Thousands join pro-Palestinian marches in several European cities","url":"https://www.morningchronicle.co.uk/Politics/775459-thousands-join-pro-palestinian-marches-in-several-european-cities.html","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Al Jazeera newsfeed page opened and read: demonstrations in NY, London, Berlin, Athens, Dublin on Oct 10 marking one year since Gaza ceasefire. AFP wire (republished, opened) corroborates with on-the-ground detail: London thousands near parliament (Palestine Coalition), ~3,500 in Berlin per police (United for Palestine), Dublin (Irish Palestine Solidarity Campaign), 20 arrests in London, small pro-Israel counter-demo, ~1,450 Palestinians killed by Israeli strikes since ceasefire per Gaza health ministry. Factual protest reporting; not an election, accusation or unverified claim. No superseding development at check time.","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T02:02:17.739Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":true,"pinUrl":"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1125618500654698525/"},{"id":"art-0022-yorkshire-tiger-enclosure-2026","slug":"man-dies-yorkshire-wildlife-park-tiger-enclosure-2026","headline":"Man Dies After Entering Tiger Enclosure at Yorkshire Wildlife Park in England","socialHeadline":"A man who entered a tiger enclosure at Yorkshire Wildlife Park was attacked and pronounced dead at the scene; police say there is no wider risk to the public","summary":"A man died on October 10 after entering the tiger enclosure at Yorkshire Wildlife Park near Doncaster, England, where he was attacked by a Siberian tiger, South Yorkshire Police said.","body":["A man died on Saturday, October 10, after entering the tiger enclosure at Yorkshire Wildlife Park near Doncaster, England. South Yorkshire Police said officers were called at 1:35pm local time following reports of a man inside the enclosure, where a Siberian tiger attacked him.","The man was pronounced dead at the scene despite the efforts of paramedics, police said. His family has been notified. The tiger was uninjured, and police said there was no wider risk to the public.","The park was evacuated and closed for the weekend following the incident. Witnesses reported seeing the man jump into the enclosure and hearing shots fired into the pen.","## Why it matters","The death is a rare and shocking incident at a major UK wildlife attraction; the park and police are expected to review how the man gained access to the enclosure."],"category":"World","tags":["UK","Wildlife","Yorkshire"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T02:02:17.739Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-yorkshire-tiger-enclosure-0-26986a1a-01a1-4360-8039-05c4474b988f.webp","alt":"Illustration of a tiger silhouette behind enclosure bars with a wildlife safety notice motif","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"CNN — Serious incident at tiger enclosure, UK park (quoting South Yorkshire Police statement in full)","url":"https://www.cnn.com/2026/10/10/uk/serious-incident-tiger-enclosure-uk-park?cid=external-feeds_iluminar_meta","role":"primary"},{"name":"People — Man mauled to death after entering tiger enclosure at Yorkshire Wildlife Park","url":"https://people.com/man-mauled-to-death-after-entering-tiger-enclosure-yorkshire-wildlife-park-zoo-england-12167813","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"CNN page opened and read, quoting South Yorkshire Police statement in full: man entered enclosure at Yorkshire Wildlife Park near Doncaster, police called 1:35pm Oct 10, Siberian tiger attacked, man pronounced dead at scene, family notified, tiger uninjured, no wider public risk, park evacuated and closed for weekend. People corroborates with witness detail (man seen jumping in, shots heard into pen). Note: pipeline's stored sourceUrl for this candidate was mismatched (pointed to an unrelated CBS video); story located via search instead. No superseding development at check time.","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T02:02:17.739Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":true,"pinUrl":"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1125618500654698572/"},{"id":"art-0023-southeast-asia-haze-2026","slug":"southeast-asia-haze-johor-schools-singapore-2026","headline":"Haze Chokes Southeast Asia: Johor Schools Shut Until Oct 16, Singapore Air Stays Unhealthy","socialHeadline":"Johor extended school closures to Oct 16 and Singapore's air stayed unhealthy as smoke from Indonesian fires drifts across the region","summary":"Johor state extended school closures to October 16 and Singapore's air quality remained in the unhealthy range as smoke haze from fires in Indonesia's Sumatra and Kalimantan drifted across Southeast Asia.","body":["The Malaysian state of Johor extended the closure of all schools and educational institutions by five more days, through October 16, 2026, as haze worsened across the region. The announcement was made late Saturday, October 10, by state education and information committee chairman Muhammad Naqib Md Ghazali, by decree of the Regent of Johor, Tunku Mahkota Ismail.","The extension follows a statewide closure on October 8-9 and affects 1,198 schools and 617,258 students, according to The Star. Students will continue home-based learning and scheduled assessments have been postponed. Officials cited forecasts that winds from Indonesia's Kalimantan between October 13 and 15 could bring more transboundary pollution; 15 areas in Malaysia recorded unhealthy Air Pollutant Index readings on Sunday morning, eight of them in Johor.","In Singapore, air quality remained in the unhealthy range across all five regions on October 11. The National Environment Agency said the 24-hour PSI ranged from 115 to 152 as of 9am Sunday, after the central region hit 192 on Friday evening — a season high — and warned the index could exceed 200, the 'very unhealthy' threshold. The haze comes from smoke drifting on east-southeasterly winds from southern Sumatra and Kalimantan. A 28-agency Haze Task Force has been convened, and the Formula 1 Singapore Grand Prix weekend is proceeding with contingency measures in place.","## Why it matters","The annual transboundary haze season is again disrupting daily life across the region, with authorities in both countries warning conditions could deteriorate further in the coming days."],"category":"World","tags":["Haze","Malaysia","Singapore","Air Quality"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T02:02:17.739Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-southeast-asia-haze-v2-0-692891b7-533d-4269-84ca-e280211fdc15.webp","alt":"Illustration of a city skyline and school building under haze bands with an air-quality gauge","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"CNA — Johor extends school closures to Oct 16 as haze worsens","url":"https://www.channelnewsasia.com/asia/malaysia-johor-school-closure-extended-oct-16-6449831","role":"primary"},{"name":"CNA — Air quality remains unhealthy across Singapore amid haze","url":"https://www.channelnewsasia.com/singapore/haze-persists-singapore-air-quality-6449771","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Combined article from two candidates covering the same transboundary haze event. CNA Johor page opened and read: closure extended Oct 12-16 announced Oct 10 by Muhammad Naqib Md Ghazali by decree of Regent Tunku Mahkota Ismail; 1,198 schools, 617,258 students (The Star via CNA); home-based learning; Kalimantan wind forecast Oct 13-15; 15 unhealthy-API areas (8 in Johor). CNA Singapore page opened and read: unhealthy across all five regions Oct 11; 24-hr PSI 115-152 (9am Sun), central region 192 Fri evening season high; NEA evening advisory Oct 10; smoke from southern Sumatra/Kalimantan; 28-agency Haze Task Force; F1 Singapore GP weekend continues with contingencies. Goody Feed corroborates Johor extension. No superseding development at check time.","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T02:02:17.739Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":true,"pinUrl":"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1125618500654698598/"},{"id":"art-0024-sauna-mental-health-research-2026","slug":"sauna-heat-therapy-mental-health-depression-research-2026","headline":"Scientists Are Putting Sauna Heat to the Test as a Possible Therapy for Depression","socialHeadline":"From floating saunas in Oslo to clinical trials in the US, researchers are testing whether heat can ease depression — early results are promising but preliminary","summary":"Researchers in Oslo and the United States are studying whether sauna and other heat therapies can help with depression and mental health. A small landmark trial found that raising body temperature reduced depressive symptoms within a week, and larger trials are now under way — though scientists stress the evidence is still early.","body":["The idea that heat can soothe the mind is ancient, but the science is only now catching up. From floating sauna villages in Oslo's harbor to clinical trials at American universities, researchers are investigating whether deliberate heat exposure could become a legitimate tool for treating depression and other mental health conditions.","In Norway, cognitive neuroscientist Eva Hilland of Oslo Metropolitan University is recruiting 50 people for a randomized controlled trial, funded by a local municipality. Instead of a laboratory, participants will visit floating saunas in Oslo's inner harbor twice a week, combining the heat sessions with simple mental health habits. The study will measure stress, well-being, sleep and more.","\"There are many knowledge gaps,\" Hilland told NPR, but the evidence she found while scanning the literature \"seemed promising. So we just saw the potential.\"","## Why heat might matter for mood","Heat appears to act on the brain through several pathways. Christopher Lowry, an integrative physiologist and neuroscientist at the University of Colorado Boulder, explains that when skin senses heat, the signals travel to a primitive part of the brain that controls cooling — a region that overlaps with a pathway involved in mood and pleasure, which is implicated in depression.","Heat also triggers an anti-inflammatory response similar to the one produced by exercise, a well-established treatment for depression. And animal studies have found that heat activates a group of serotonin neurons that may provide stress resilience and antidepressant effects, Lowry said.","The strongest human data come from a small landmark trial published a decade ago by a team at the University of Wisconsin-Madison. In that study, 30 people with depression were randomly assigned to either spend about two hours in a whole-body infrared device that raised their body temperature to about 38.5°C, or to a sham treatment. Within a week, a majority of the treated group had experienced a 50% reduction in symptoms, and the effect persisted through a six-week follow-up.","## A 'thermoregulatory workout'","Clinical psychologist Ashley Mason of the University of California, San Francisco, was drawn into the field by those findings. She noticed an intriguing pattern: people with depression tend to have difficulty with thermoregulation. \"What we know from a bunch of literature is that depressed people seem to run hot,\" she said. Her lab has tracked body temperature against depressive symptoms in wearable-device data from close to 20,000 people, finding that worse symptoms correlated with higher skin temperature and less daily temperature fluctuation.","Heating the body may function like a \"thermoregulatory workout,\" Mason says — training the system to cool down more efficiently afterward. She has run two small pilot trials combining eight weeks of cognitive behavioral therapy with four sessions in an infrared hyperthermia machine; in both studies, most participants were in remission from depression by the end. Her team is now running the same protocol in a larger pool of patients at UCSF, Harvard and the Cleveland Clinic, funded by the National Institutes of Health and others.","## Early days","Scientists are careful to temper expectations. The evidence base largely rests on animal studies, cell models and a small number of human trials, most without strict control groups. Mason stresses that the pilot results are preliminary — the studies were not powered to show the treatments were effective — but they lay the groundwork for the larger, well-controlled trials that could.","\"Heat does seem to be a promising therapy, but we're very much at the beginning of this research,\" she said. If future studies confirm the effect, heat therapy could earn a place alongside other non-pharmacological approaches for mental health, like exercise — \"a seat at the table\" for people whose depression has resisted other treatments, as Mason put it."],"category":"Health","tags":["Mental Health","Depression","Sauna","NPR","Science"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-sauna-mental-health-0-0-21af18cd-d994-43b4-b6b8-8cf0c0d7285f.webp","alt":"Flat illustration of a wooden sauna interior with heat waves, a thermometer, moon and heart icons","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"NPR — 'From floating saunas to clinical trials: How heat might help mental health' (Siv Dolmen, 2026-10-05)","url":"https://kvcr.org/news/npr-top-stories/2026-10-05/sauna-heat-therapy-mental-health-depression","role":"primary"},{"name":"NPR member stations (KTTZ, WEXT, WKYU) — same reporting, independent syndication","url":"https://radio.kttz.org/2026-10-05/from-floating-saunas-to-clinical-trials-how-heat-might-help-mental-health","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"NPR (2026-10-05) reporting verified: Hilland/OsloMet 50-person RCT (Oslo harbor floating saunas), Lowry/UC Boulder mechanisms, Wisconsin 30-person trial (38.5°C, majority 50% sympt","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0025-shelton-gea-shanghai-masters-2026","slug":"ben-shelton-arthur-gea-shanghai-masters-upset-2026","headline":"\"I Got Outplayed\": Ben Shelton Falls to France's Arthur Gea in Shanghai Masters Upset","socialHeadline":"World No. 4 Ben Shelton was stunned 7-6(5), 7-6(3) by 21-year-old Arthur Gea in the third round of the Shanghai Masters — the Frenchman's first win over a top-10 player","summary":"US Open finalist Ben Shelton was knocked out of the Shanghai Masters on Sunday, losing 7-6(5), 7-6(3) to France's Arthur Gea in the third round. The world No. 56 claimed the biggest win of his career, while Shelton admitted he had been outplayed.","body":["Ben Shelton's Shanghai Masters campaign ended in the third round on Sunday as the world No. 4 fell 7-6(5), 7-6(3) to France's Arthur Gea, according to Reuters. It was the 21-year-old Frenchman's first victory over a top-10 player and one of the biggest upsets of the 2026 season.","Both sets were decided in tiebreaks. Shelton, whose powerful left-handed serve is usually his biggest weapon, managed just 63% of points behind his first delivery as Gea's disciplined returning kept him under constant pressure. The American faced three match points at 6-3 in the second-set tiebreaker; Gea converted the first.","## Shelton's honest assessment","Shelton was candid after the defeat. \"I mean, I got outplayed today. The guy played better than me,\" he told reporters, according to Reuters. He pointed to his lack of preparation since September's US Open final, where he lost to Alexander Zverev: \"A hundred percent, I would have liked to have come over here earlier and be prepared and have already dealt with the jet lag by the time I was playing here in the Shanghai Masters.\"","The 24-year-old has barely played since New York, withdrawing from the Japan Open in Tokyo over fitness concerns. \"My body wasn't ready. I wasn't physically ready to play in Tokyo. That's just the way this tour is sometimes,\" he said.","Shelton, who won his first match in Shanghai on his 24th birthday, now turns his focus to the season-ending ATP Finals in Turin next month. \"Obviously I want to be prepared and playing some of my best tennis when I get there,\" he added. \"Three tournaments left to finish the year, which has been a very up and down year, but a great year, on a high note.\"","## A breakthrough for Gea","Gea, ranked 56th in the world, was delighted with a result he called special. \"I'm practicing hard every day since the beginning of the year to win against those guys,\" he said. \"Of course, when you win, it is always special. But, yeah, I was prepared and I was confident before the match.\"","The Frenchman now faces either Jakub Mensik or Francisco Cerundolo for a place in the quarter-finals.","Elsewhere on Sunday, 26th seed Karen Khachanov beat Adrian Mannarino 6-2, 6-4, while top seed and US Open champion Alexander Zverev was scheduled for a night match against Quentin Halys. No. 1-ranked Jannik Sinner withdrew from Shanghai earlier in the week, announcing he is taking the rest of 2026 off because of a right knee injury, the Associated Press reported."],"category":"Sports","tags":["Tennis","ATP","Shanghai Masters","Ben Shelton","Arthur Gea"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-shelton-shanghai-upset-0-0-c7c3c6b4-0006-4a48-aa56-e6e2df9bce09.webp","alt":"Flat illustration of a tennis court with a racket, ball and scoreboard showing two 7-6 sets","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Reuters — 'Gea sends Shelton crashing out of Shanghai' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/sports/tennis/gea-sends-shelton-crashing-out-shanghai-2026-10-11/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Associated Press, via Sportsnet — 'Shelton beaten by Gea in Shanghai Masters R3' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.sportsnet.ca/atp/article/ben-shelton-ousted-in-third-round-of-shanghai-masters/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Reuters (2026-10-11) verified: 7-6(5), 7-6(3), third round, Shanghai, Sunday; world No","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0026-super-el-nino-2026-record-2026","slug":"super-el-nino-2026-record-climate-warming-2026","headline":"Scientists Track a Potentially Record 'Super El Niño' as a Warming World Fuels the Extremes","socialHeadline":"The 2026 El Niño is tracking hotter than the great events of 1997 and 2015 at the same point in the year — and scientists say it could push global temperatures to new records","summary":"The El Niño building across the Pacific in 2026 is on track to be one of the strongest ever recorded, climate scientists say, with ocean temperatures already running hotter than the famous super El Niños of 1997 and 2015. Researchers warn it could drive record global heat in 2026 and 2027, amplified by the background of human-caused warming.","body":["The warming of the equatorial Pacific known as El Niño is developing into something extraordinary in 2026, and scientists are warning that it could shatter records. Analyses of ocean temperatures suggest the event is already tracking above the great El Niños of 1997 and 2015 at the same point in their development.","\"No El Niño in the modern record has run this warm this early in its development,\" Berkeley Earth climate scientist Zeke Hausfather and chief scientist Robert Rohde wrote in a July 2026 temperature update. They estimate sea surface temperatures at the event's peak in December could run roughly 4°C above average in the key Niño regions — \"blowing the previous record out of the water.\"","## What the agencies say","The UK Met Office has called the developing event \"unprecedented,\" with its long-range GloSea forecast system showing sea surface temperatures in the Niño 3.4 region exceeding 3°C above normal in the coming months. Professor Adam Scaife, the Met Office's head of long-range forecasting, said he had \"never seen an El Niño signal this intense in our forecasts.\"","The World Meteorological Organization has warned the phenomenon will last until at least February, with severe consequences for weather worldwide, according to Wired's September reporting.","## Why it matters","El Niños are a natural part of the climate cycle, but they now play out against a planet already warmed by greenhouse gases — and that makes them more destructive. The Met Office notes that the Indian summer monsoon is already running well below normal rainfall, with Central America, western Pacific nations and tropical South America also at risk of low rainfall. El Niño also tends to suppress Atlantic hurricanes by increasing wind shear; consistent with that pattern, there have been only three Atlantic storms so far this season, though the agency cautions that a single large hurricane can still cause devastation.","For global temperatures, the outlook is stark. Rohde said during a July press briefing that it was \"now more likely than not\" that the extraordinary El Niño would bring record warmth in 2026 and \"much stronger warmth\" in 2027. Some analyses suggest the global average could climb to around 1.7°C above preindustrial levels by 2027 — above the 1.5°C threshold long treated as a guardrail.","## The climate connection","That is the focus of new reporting from Wired on how the 2026 super El Niño and climate change are related: El Niño is no longer just a temporary fluctuation but a force whose variability is intensified by a warming world, compounding cascading impacts.","The warming will not last forever — Rohde expects 2028 to be cooler as the event subsides. But the background trend keeps climbing. \"Human emissions are adding a permanent El Niño worth of heat to the climate system each decade,\" Hausfather told The Washington Post. Even as El Niño's direct influence fades, the heat it borrows against the future does not fully return."],"category":"Science","tags":["Climate","El Niño","Global Warming","Weather","Berkeley Earth"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-super-el-nino-2026-0-0-94d82c5e-c06d-464f-ace4-6385095cae64.webp","alt":"Flat illustration of a Pacific Ocean world map with warm red current arrows, a rising thermometer and storm clouds","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Wired — 'How the 2026 Super El Niño and Climate Change Are Related' (2026-10-11, discovery lead)","url":"https://metaviews.ca/signal/2026-09-05-070624-super-el-nino-black-sea-grain-war-food-markets/","role":"corroboration"},{"name":"UK Met Office — 'An unprecedented El Niño and its implications for the weather forecast' (official press release, 2026-08-24)","url":"https://www.wired-gov.net/wg/news.nsf/articles/An+unprecedented+El+Ni%C3%B1o+and+its+implications+for+the+weather+forecast+24082026151515","role":"primary"},{"name":"Gizmodo reporting Berkeley Earth July 2026 temperature update (Hausfather, Rohde)","url":"https://gizmodo.com/super-el-nino-could-push-earths-temperature-13-years-ahead-of-the-current-warming-trend-2000798669","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Wired 2026-10-11 story (discovery lead) corroborated by: Met Office official press release (2026-08-24, 'unprecedented', Nino3.4 >3°C, Prof Scaife quote), Berkeley Earth July updat","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0027-singapore-sparkletots-20-million-2026","slug":"singapore-pcf-sparkletots-staff-training-20-million-2027","headline":"Singapore's Largest Preschool Operator to Double Teacher Training Spend to S$20 Million","socialHeadline":"PCF Sparkletots will invest S$20 million in staff development over three years from 2027 and offer Chinese, Malay and Tamil in all its preschools — announced at its 40th anniversary celebrations","summary":"Singapore's largest preschool operator, PCF Sparkletots, will double its investment in staff development to S$20 million over three years from 2027, the organization announced on Sunday at a family day event at Mandai Wildlife Reserve marking its 40th anniversary.","body":["PCF Sparkletots, Singapore's largest preschool operator, will double what it spends on training its teachers to S$20 million over the next three years, the PAP Community Foundation (PCF) announced on Sunday at a family day event at Mandai Wildlife Reserve celebrating the foundation's 40th anniversary.","The investment will begin from 2027 and goes alongside a plan to offer Chinese, Malay and Tamil in all its preschools from 2027 where there is demand, plus an enhanced centralized model to cut administrative work across its centres so educators can spend more time with children and teaching.","## Four decades of PCF","Deputy Prime Minister Gan Kim Yong, who attended as guest of honour, said PCF had over 40 years supported more than a million children, served some 30,000 seniors, and empowered more than 46,000 vulnerable beneficiaries.","PCF today operates close to 350 preschool centres, making it Singapore's largest preschool operator. It is also the country's third-largest senior care provider, with 11 senior care centres and nine active ageing centres.","## Why teachers matter","PCF Council of Management chairperson Josephine Teo, who is also Singapore's Minister for Digital Development and Information, said the investment reflected the outsized role teachers play in children's learning: parents entrust the operator with their children's formative years, so it must develop its teachers to help them be more effective and give every child a strong start.","The announcement fits a longer shift in Singapore's early childhood sector, where anchor operators like PCF Sparkletots have moved from simply expanding centre numbers to upgrading teacher quality and curriculum — a direction the Early Childhood Development Agency has encouraged to keep fees affordable while raising standards."],"category":"World","tags":["Singapore","Education","Preschool","PCF Sparkletots","Asia"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-sparkletots-preschool-0-0-fba64f7b-c021-42c6-bf6b-c3abbb8bcde0.webp","alt":"Flat illustration of a preschool classroom with a teacher and faceless geometric children, crayons and blocks","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"The Straits Times, via Nestia — 'PCF Sparkletots to double staff development spending to $20m' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://news.nestia.com/detail_share/14191475?media_type=1","role":"primary"},{"name":"The Straits Times, via Etleboro — same announcement (2026-10-11)","url":"https://etleboro.org/g/b894799558b53d0408036a674e9ab517en/pcf-sparkletots-to-double-staff-development-spending-to-$20m-ease-teachers’-admin-workload","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Straits Times (2026-10-11) verified via two independent syndication mirrors: S$20m over 3 years from 2027, announced Oct 11 at Mandai Wildlife Reserve family day (40th anniversary)","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0028-redwoods-heat-stress-study-2026","slug":"california-redwoods-heat-stress-photosynthesis-study-2026","headline":"California's Giant Redwoods Are Getting 'Heatstroke', a New Study Finds","socialHeadline":"When temperatures spiked, the world's tallest trees slowed photosynthesis — the process that feeds them. UC Davis researchers say the findings raise alarms for the forests' future in a warming climate","summary":"California's iconic coast redwoods — the tallest trees on Earth — slow the very process that feeds them when temperatures spike, according to a new University of California, Davis study. The findings, the first to measure heat's effect on redwood photosynthesis, raise concerns about the future of the forests as heatwaves grow more intense.","body":["The world's tallest trees are struggling to stay cool. When air temperatures topped 86°F in a Mendocino County redwood forest during the summers of 2022 and 2024, some redwood leaves ran nearly 20°F hotter than the air — a sign of stress that researchers had never fully measured before.","The UC Davis study, led by PhD candidate Lily Klinek of the Plant Optics Lab in the Department of Plant Sciences and published in JGR Biogeosciences, tracked the trees over three summers. It found that under heat stress, coast redwoods slow photosynthesis — the chemical reaction that converts sunlight, water and carbon dioxide into the carbon they need to grow. \"It's as if the trees slow their 'breathing' and, as a result, their 'eating,'\" the researchers explain.","\"The leaves aren't able to cool down,\" Klinek said — which suggests they closed their stomata, the tiny pores that take in carbon dioxide, to conserve water. Follow-up lab tests at temperatures up to 110°F confirmed that photosynthesis was reduced even when the leaves had plenty of water and kept their stomata open.","## Why redwoods are vulnerable","Redwoods evolved for cool coastal conditions, with average temperatures around 59°F. They also depend on coastal fog, which acts as a natural air conditioner. As heat spikes burn off that fog, the trees lose a key source of moisture — exactly when they need it most.","The concern is greatest for redwood forests in already vulnerable central, southern and eastern parts of their range. \"We don't know what the upper temperature thresholds are for redwood photosynthesis and mortality,\" Klinek said. \"With this work, we see there's a significant impact of heat on photosynthesis and physiology. That's an important start for figuring out what parts of the redwood range are at risk.\"","There is a sliver of good news: the trees the team studied did not lose their capacity to photosynthesize after the heat passed. \"Right now the temperatures are coming back to normal in the fall and winter and letting the trees recover,\" Klinek said. \"But in five or 10 years, if temperatures are even hotter and heat waves are even more frequent, we don't really know if there would be a recovery.\"","Independent experts share the concern. UC Berkeley plant ecophysiologist Todd Dawson, who did not take part in the study, called it \"a double whammy\": \"They're running out of water and also getting this heat stress.\" He noted redwoods are adapted to a narrow band of 8 to 27°C, and that the coastal fog they rely on has declined by 30 to 40 percent.","The study's authors include Troy Magney, Jessie Au and Milagros Rodriguez-Caton of UC Davis, Mukund Palat Rao of Columbia University, Lauren Fety of The Conservation Fund and George Koch of Northern Arizona University. It was funded by the National Science Foundation and California Forestry and Fire Protection, in cooperation with The Conservation Fund."],"category":"Science","tags":["Climate","Redwoods","California","Forests","UC Davis"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-redwoods-heat-stress-0-0-e0046d25-850a-41e1-880b-61ee372de4b7.webp","alt":"Flat illustration of tall redwood trees beside a rising thermometer, a blazing sun and a magnified leaf","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"UC Davis — 'Coast Redwoods Slow Their Breathing and Eating When Temperatures Spike' (official, 2026)","url":"https://www.ucdavis.edu/climate/news/coast-redwoods-slow-their-breathing-and-eating-when-temperatures-spike","role":"primary"},{"name":"Wired — 'California's Tallest and Most Iconic Trees Are Getting Heatstroke' (2026-10-11, discovery lead)","url":"https://www.scientificinquirer.com/2026/10/06/coast-redwoods-slow-their-breathing-and-eating-when-temperatures-spike/","role":"corroboration"},{"name":"Phys.org — 'Coast redwoods slow their breathing and eating when temperatures spike' (2026-09)","url":"https://phys.org/news/2026-09-coast-redwoods-temperatures-spike.html?deviceType=mobile","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"UC Davis official page verified: Klinek (PhD candidate, Plant Optics Lab) lead author, JGR Biogeosciences, first study of heat on coast redwood photosynthesis, three summers in Men","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0029-iran-shopkeepers-war-economy-2026","slug":"iran-shopkeepers-economy-war-inflation-tehran-2026","headline":"\"Going Bankrupt\": Iran's Shopkeepers Struggle as War Wrecks the Economy","socialHeadline":"At Tehran's Tajrish bazaar, customers who once bought nuts by the kilo now buy by the handful. With inflation near 90% and the currency collapsing, merchants say they are fighting for survival","summary":"At the historic Tajrish bazaar in northern Tehran, the stalls are quieter than they used to be. Shoppers who once bought nuts by the kilogram now buy a half-kilo or less, as soaring prices driven by the US-Iran war eat into sales. Across the commercial district, many merchants say they are fighting for survival.","body":["Where fragrant herbs and spices once drew crowds through the narrow paths of the Tajrish bazaar, shops now sit mostly empty, according to an AFP dispatch carried by France 24. Nasir, a 61-year-old fruit and nut seller, said customers who \"used to buy two to five kilograms\" now buy one kilogram or half. \"Prices are truly high. We all know it, and it would be a lie to say otherwise,\" he said.","The pressure comes from a war that began in February, the dispatch reports, involving US-Israeli attacks and an American blockade of Iran's ports — on top of years of sanctions that had already battered the economy.","## Numbers in freefall","Official figures cited in the dispatch paint a bleak picture. Inflation ran at nearly 90% year-on-year in September, and food prices have more than doubled since last year. Gross domestic product contracted 10.1% year-on-year between late March and late June, according to official data.","The currency has collapsed with it: the rial traded at around 2.7 million to the dollar on the unofficial market in the past week, compared with about 1.7 million before the war. The minimum monthly wage, worth around $120 a year ago, has fallen to $65.","## 'A desperate, last-ditch struggle'","Ali Nowruzi, 36, who runs a sportswear shop in the bazaar, described the squeeze from both ends: \"It is a desperate, last-ditch struggle. Manufacturers are going bankrupt, laying off staff and closing shops, and the impact inevitably reaches us.\" He now orders only a few items for display, he said, so the shelves do not look as bare as his warehouse, which lies empty for lack of demand.","\"We have absolutely no plan for the future. When people don't come to buy… it effectively spells bankruptcy for the business,\" he said, citing rising rent and utility bills. \"We just need some stability.\"","The strain reaches far beyond the bazaar. Azadeh, a 45-year-old woman currently out of work, said a kitchen cloth that cost her 22 cents a few months ago now costs $1.10 — \"prices haven't just gone up, they've truly skyrocketed,\" she said. She has stopped buying some fruits and can no longer afford holidays. Car mechanic Mojtaba Rezaei, 57, told AFP his customers had \"dropped to a tenth of what it was\" because goods now cost two or three times as much — \"I actually feel embarrassed telling prices to customers.\"","Iran's economy minister has rejected predictions of an imminent economic collapse, accusing the country's foes of trying to fuel public anxiety and drive up exchange rates, according to the dispatch.","Independent reporting backs the broader trend: Euronews interviews with Iranians describe emptied wallets and collapsing purchasing power since the war began, while financial analysis has noted real-wage pressure across the region as the conflict disrupts energy and trade flows."],"category":"World","tags":["Iran","Economy","Inflation","Middle East","AFP"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-iran-bazaar-economy-0-0-7cad5538-a19c-4b9e-bc6d-cd6f90b6ae7a.webp","alt":"Flat illustration of a covered bazaar with market stalls, a rising price tag and a declining currency graph","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"AFP, via France 24 — 'Going bankrupt': Iran shopkeepers struggle as war dims demand (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.newsbeep.com/766078/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Euronews — 'The country is falling apart': Iranians tell how war emptied their wallets (2026-09)","url":"https://dailyguardian.eu/iranians-tell-euronews-how-war-emptied-their-wallets/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"AFP dispatch (via France 24 RSS, mirrored NewsBeep) verified: Tajrish bazaar, Tehran; Nasir (61) nut seller; war began February (US-Israeli attacks + US blockade of ports, attribut","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T10:21:25Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","body":["Pope Leo XIV announced on Sunday that he will undergo surgery this week after doctors discovered a nodule on his lung, telling thousands gathered in St Peter's Square for the weekly Angelus that the growth was detected at what he described as a very early stage.","The 71-year-old pontiff said his doctors had recommended the operation and that he had decided to go ahead with it, asking the crowd for their prayers. The announcement, made in person from the window of the Apostolic Palace, was his first public disclosure of a health issue since his election.","Vatican spokesman Matteo Bruni confirmed that the surgery is scheduled for the first days of the week and is expected to take place at Rome's Gemelli Hospital, the facility that has treated popes for decades. Recovery is expected to take about a week, the Vatican said.","Officials stressed that the nodule is localized and was caught early. The pope, who turned 71 this year, has had no previously known health problems during his pontificate.","The announcement raises questions about the pope's upcoming travel plans, including a scheduled trip to Latin America from November 6 to 17. The Vatican has not said whether the itinerary will be affected.","The news drew immediate reaction from Catholic leaders and heads of state, with messages of support arriving from around the world within hours of the Angelus address."],"breaking":false,"category":"World","editorPick":false,"headline":"Pope Leo XIV to Undergo Lung Surgery This Week After Nodule Found at 'Very Early Stage'","id":"art-0030-pope-leo-lung-surgery-2026","image":{"alt":"Flat editorial illustration of St Peter's Basilica dome silhouette with a dove and a subtle medical cross motif","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration","src":"/images/media-generation-nv-pope-leo-surgery-20261011.webp"},"pinUrl":"","pinned":false,"publishedAt":"2026-10-11T13:45:00Z","slug":"pope-leo-xiv-lung-surgery-nodule-gemelli-2026","socialHeadline":"Pope Leo XIV announces lung surgery this week after doctors find early-stage nodule","sources":[{"name":"Associated Press — 'Pope Leo XIV says he will undergo surgery this week' (2026-10-11)","role":"primary","url":"https://gray-wowt-prod.gtv-cdn.com/2026/10/11/pope-leo-xiv-says-he-will-undergo-surgery-heres-why/"},{"name":"NPR — 'Pope Leo XIV to undergo lung surgery this week' (2026-10-11)","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.whro.org/2026-10-11/pope-leo-xiv-to-undergo-lung-surgery-this-week"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","summary":"Pope Leo XIV told crowds in St Peter's Square on Sunday that doctors found a localized nodule on his lung and advised surgery. The Vatican says the operation will take place in the coming days at Rome's Gemelli Hospital, with about a week of recovery expected.","tags":["Pope Leo XIV","Vatican","Health","Catholic Church","Rome"],"verification":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:00Z","chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"eventConfirmed":true,"imageChecked":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"notes":"Pope's own Oct 11 Angelus announcement (Vatican) verified via AP and NPR page reads: localized lung nodule at very early stage; surgery first days of the week at Rome's Gemelli Hospital; ~1 week recovery; Vatican spokesman Matteo Bruni confirmation; pope aged 71, no known prior health issues.","primarySourceFound":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","supersededChecked":true}},{"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","body":["At least 109 migrants, including 15 children, have died after a boat carrying about 350 people capsized off the coast of Djibouti, the International Organization for Migration said on Sunday.","The vessel went down during the night of October 8-9 near Guhere, north of the town of Obock, while sailing from Djibouti toward Yemen, according to the IOM. The agency said 109 bodies had been recovered so far: 52 men, 42 women and 15 children, nine of them girls and six boys. More than 116 people were still missing, and over 80 survivors — all Ethiopian nationals — had been pulled from the water.","IOM teams are on the ground working alongside Djiboutian authorities, and survivors are being assisted at the agency's migrant response centre in Obock. \"This is a devastating loss of life,\" the IOM's chief of mission in Djibouti, Alexandre Coissac, said. Search and rescue operations were continuing on Sunday.","The Djibouti-Yemen crossing is one of the world's busiest and most perilous migration corridors, used each year by tens of thousands of people — many from Ethiopia — attempting to reach Gulf states in search of work. Overloaded, unseaworthy boats make the journey routinely deadly; exact passenger counts often vary in the first hours after a disaster, with some outlets reporting between 305 and 350 people aboard this vessel."],"breaking":false,"category":"World","editorPick":false,"headline":"109 Dead, Including 15 Children, After Migrant Boat Capsizes Off Djibouti, UN Agency Says","id":"art-0031-djibouti-migrant-boat-2026","image":{"alt":"Flat editorial illustration of dark sea waves with a lifebuoy and a map pin marking Djibouti, in somber navy tones","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration","src":"/images/media-generation-nv-djibouti-boat-tragedy-20261011.webp"},"pinUrl":"","pinned":false,"publishedAt":"2026-10-11T13:45:00Z","slug":"djibouti-migrant-boat-capsizes-109-dead-iom-2026","socialHeadline":"At least 109 migrants dead after boat capsizes off Djibouti, IOM says","sources":[{"name":"Reuters — '109 migrants, including 15 children, dead after boat off Djibouti-Yemen capsize